{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>May El hear</b> — He returns to speak of his enemies, who terrify in their dwelling." "<b>and answer them</b> — From the root of עני ידלדלם (Afflict, impoverish them). And the correct in my eyes: He will answer through them, like לא נגענוך (We did not touch you), which is נגענו בך (We touched you)." "<b>who sits enthroned of old</b> — like שוכן (dweller); He will answer them in truth." "<b>who have no changes</b> — that their lot will change from good to evil." "<b>and do not fear Elohim</b> — that it is in His hand to change me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {4 "Reading יחליפני (change me) as in the received text; some witnesses may read differently."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:01.461489355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}